# The Aven's enters trigger targets Bot2's Lightning Bolt. Bot2 responds by countering its own Bolt with Counterspell, so
# (Bot2 first lets the Aven resolve, so the trigger is on the stack with the Bolt as its target) the target is illegal when the trigger resolves (CR 608.2b) and nothing is exiled or plotted: the Bolt is in the
# graveyard, not in exile, and cannot be cast again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl x3
Aven Interrupter
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Sapphire x2
Lightning Bolt
Counterspell
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Aven Interrupter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Life = 20
